    "closure_derivation": "The frozen build closure is the makefile plus every tracked file under the build-input directories src/, tilesets/ and tools/, minus closure_exclusions. An exclusion is valid only if no build-relevant token references it: (1) makefile tokens after dropping # comments and joining continuations, matched word-bounded by path, basename or module stem, with $(wildcard ...) arguments treated as fnmatch globs and a bare % prerequisite expanded with the target pattern suffix; (2) import and from-import module names in non-excluded tools/*.py; (3) include and incbin directive targets in src/*.z80 and src/*.inc. Free text in comments, strings and docstrings is never matched. Every src include/incbin target must be a closure path under src/ or a generated obj/gb/ path, and every prerequisite of a rule for $(title).gb or obj/gb/ must be a make variable, an obj/gb/ path, a path under src/, tilesets/ or tools/, or a closure path. verify-libbet-admission.py --derive-closure SRC_DIR re-derives this from a source tree; required CI, which has no source tree, detects a dropped closure entry through the EXPECTED_CLOSURE_SHA256 constant.",
